      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Does each failure become **exactly one** error log, linked to the trace?\n**The rule being proven:** the span keeps only the error **type** (`exception.type`); the **message** and the **stack** go to **one** correlated error log. Why: messages can hold sensitive data and are expensive to index in a trace; in the log they are searchable and under controlled retention. Here we look only at the **error logs** in Loki: how many have a `trace_id`, who writes them and whether any error appears twice. An error log from an **unsampled** span has a valid `trace_id` that Tempo does not have, so its trace link opens an empty trace. Terms: [0. Start here](/d/demo-otel-start).",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "description": "Fraction of error logs with a `trace_id`. **Target: 100%.** Known cause of a lower value: Python's `uvicorn.error` (see the number next to it).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 1,
          "noValue": "0",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red"
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.9
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.999
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"demo-(${lang:pipe})-(api|backend|worker)\", service_name=~\"${service:pipe}\"} | severity_number >= 17 | trace_id != \"\" [$__range])) / sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"demo-(${lang:pipe})-(api|backend|worker)\", service_name=~\"${service:pipe}\"} | severity_number >= 17 [$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
